#{[{:activity/expected-seconds 420.0 :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060557} :activity/id #uuid "5783ad54-a014-54a2-bf03-179b532b54dc" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050743 :topic/id #uuid "62da5cd1-bbc7-584a-ba89-8e03cd9c311f" :topic/math-academy-id 252} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060557 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060985 :tutorial/content "A conditional statement $A \\Rightarrow B$ has three related logical forms:\n\n- the **converse:** $B \\Rightarrow A$\n\n- the **inverse:** $\\lnot A \\Rightarrow \\lnot B$\n\n- the **contrapositive:** $\\lnot B \\Rightarrow \\lnot A$\n\nFor example, consider the following true statement:\n\n$\\qquad$ If I am George Washington, then I am an American.\n\nHere, the antecedent is $A=$ \"I am George Washington,\" and the consequent is $B=$ \"I am an American.\"\n\n- The *converse* is \"If I am an American, then I am George Washington.\"\n\n- The *inverse* is \"If I am not George Washington, then I am not an American.\"\n\n- The *contrapositive* is \"If I am not an American, then I am not George Washington.\"\n\nAs we can see from the statements above, only the contrapositive is also true." :tutorial/id #uuid "f381549b-ee22-54fc-8819-f65677237a08" :tutorial/math-academy-id 7979 :tutorial/title "Introduction"} :step/id #uuid "359b59a3-ea7e-534e-bcef-10e9ba22f6e5" :step/math-academy-id 143402 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060558}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060558 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059691 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059413 :question/id #uuid "9f3fe8eb-f539-539e-96c6-33b6a238fc82" :question/math-academy-id "e-12711"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ec5acb94-b33a-5921-b761-6f78db3f25f7" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050360}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060111} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060422} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186378313} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186379288} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186380207} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186404204} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186404211} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186573872} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186573941}] :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Converse of a Statement"} :step/id #uuid "e2eb4f41-af42-517b-80cc-4e15c689de2d" :step/math-academy-id 143403 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060559}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060559 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059692 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059412 :question/id #uuid "144f352c-5696-5ad3-841f-3a6a1cf2e5f2" :question/math-academy-id "e-12710"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "dffa4760-00cb-5395-8fab-dc7f9fe20597" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048349}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060110} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060413} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186379274} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186379281} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186380200} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186399524} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186399545} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186407669} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186407670} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186573918}] :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Inverse of a Statement"} :step/id #uuid "c85a942c-f9af-53b4-b1da-fa03e8854a2d" :step/math-academy-id 143406 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060560}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060560 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059693 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059414 :question/id #uuid "9e1fa00b-8e51-5689-959d-049df21077bd" :question/math-academy-id "e-12712"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7f58ec96-53b3-5317-9801-c730728f32c6" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060112} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060414} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186378320} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186379295} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186379302} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186386216} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186407671} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186573899}] :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Contrapositive of a Statement"} :step/id #uuid "a0cda17a-d96e-5ea8-bb9e-ccd79d7904dc" :step/math-academy-id 143409 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060561}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060561 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060986 :tutorial/content "In general, we have the following facts:\n\n- The contrapositive is logically equivalent to the original statement:\n\n$$\n\\underbrace{A \\Rightarrow B}_{\\textrm{original}} \\equiv \\underbrace{\\neg B \\Rightarrow \\neg A}_{\\textrm{contrapositive}}\n$$\n\n- The inverse and the converse are logically equivalent to each other but not to the original statement:\n\n$$\n\\underbrace{\\neg A \\Rightarrow \\neg B}_{\\textrm{inverse}} \\equiv \\underbrace{B \\Rightarrow A}_{\\textrm{converse}}\n$$\n\nWe can prove these results using a truth table, as shown below:\n\n| $\\,A\\,$ | $\\,B\\,$ | $\\, A \\Rightarrow B \\,$ | $\\, \\neg A \\Rightarrow \\neg B \\,$ | $\\, B \\Rightarrow A \\,$ | $\\, \\neg B \\Rightarrow \\neg A \\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\textrm T$ | $\\textrm T$ | $\\color{blue} \\textrm T$ | $\\color{red} \\textrm T$ | $\\color{red} \\textrm T$ | $\\color{blue} \\textrm T$ |\n| $\\textrm T$ | $\\textrm F$ | $\\color{blue} \\textrm F$ | $\\color{red} \\textrm T$ | $\\color{red} \\textrm T$ | $\\color{blue} \\textrm F$ |\n| $\\textrm F$ | $\\textrm T$ | $\\color{blue} \\textrm T$ | $\\color{red} \\textrm F$ | $\\color{red} \\textrm F$ | $\\color{blue} \\textrm T$ |\n| $\\textrm F$ | $\\textrm F$ | $\\color{blue} \\textrm T$ | $\\color{red} \\textrm T$ | $\\color{red} \\textrm T$ | $\\color{blue} \\textrm T$ |\n\nThis can be visualized using the following diagram.\n\n![](images/d9/d946d2a81d46cbde934ebbab54f9b69b514092e02da4f8a3b79768f218929449.png)" :tutorial/id #uuid "5bbcfb96-5707-521a-bea1-559cf154472f" :tutorial/math-academy-id 7980 :tutorial/title "Logically Equivalent Conditional Statements"} :step/id #uuid "74a00ea0-ef35-56ab-86b6-44c08bc91491" :step/math-academy-id 143412 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060562}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060562 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059694 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059415 :question/id #uuid "31e2f48c-65cc-53c3-b34c-70e2c53a9274" :question/math-academy-id "e-12713"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "93d3501b-96ef-5fbd-9d93-788021156ddb" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049805}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060113} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060415} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186378327} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186379309} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186380214} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186380221} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186407667} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186407668}] :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Logically Equivalent Statements"} :step/id #uuid "f375663a-5188-59fe-b4e2-7d315657f509" :step/math-academy-id 143413}] :activity/title "Converse, Inverse, and Contrapositive" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :activity.type/lesson} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186059930}] [{:activity/course {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186046673} :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186407672} :activity/id #uuid "b3117d1c-d259-5ca7-8dcf-c2ea2b248c11" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050743 :topic/id #uuid "62da5cd1-bbc7-584a-ba89-8e03cd9c311f" :topic/math-academy-id 252} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186407672 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186407668 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "915545ce-c423-5da4-91dc-290407b53372" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473446} {:answer/id #uuid "8f85f5bf-c4f5-5094-8323-a67c9fa53bc5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473447}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186473446} :answer-field/id #uuid "3898d384-3181-550c-8344-cde598e23fab" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474118} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b3b76f77-9332-57a9-afde-de8d55488d37" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473448} {:answer/id #uuid "bee0a274-ed2c-5c01-b766-3ba728c9c822" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473449}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186473448} :answer-field/id #uuid "ffea5c3f-a699-5852-afaa-150401a98451" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474119} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f4f64a71-8fa0-502d-8cc4-7ae6c1d1511b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473450} {:answer/id #uuid "80e07b43-5cc7-5ba7-bb18-f3644b44ddf8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473451}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186473451} :answer-field/id #uuid "65a10d53-1347-54fd-b77a-a4d9ac2a0931" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474120}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "41c661ac-cdce-5cf9-814b-cfcfe49d2399" :question/math-academy-id "q-82665" :question/problem "$\\,$ **If** you are sick, **then** you are not going to school.\n\nWhich of the following statements are equivalent to the conditional statement above?\n- **I.** If you are not going to school, then you are sick.\n- **II.** If you are not sick, then you are going to school.\n- **III.** If you are going to school, then you are not sick.\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's recall the following facts:\n\n- The contrapositive is logically equivalent to the original statement.\n\n- The inverse and the converse are logically equivalent to each other, but not to the original statement.\n\n![](images/0d/0deb19675402bf931111bb80cb616682aac08491b5cd3e1ab5812da05b6df8a8.png)\n\nSo, we are looking for the contrapositive.\n\n- Statement I is the converse, not the contrapositive. $\\,\\times $\n\n- Statement II is the inverse, not the contrapositive. $\\,\\times $\n\n- Statement III is the contrapositive. $\\,✓$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\""} :step/id #uuid "19a46d5b-7cad-5c8f-bf15-b2f08d43ce6e" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186407673}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186407673 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186407670 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1f50cc62-1ef8-5d26-94fe-19cc0496e946" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "If $6$ is not even, then $3$ divides $6.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186407639} {:answer/id #uuid "55a2ad61-ddd6-50db-8998-9ea2b6f81055" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "If $3$ doesn't divide $6,$ then $6$ is not even." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186407646} {:answer/id #uuid "96b53686-f3f0-55fa-86a0-e4e41c9ed2c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "If $3$ divides $6,$ then $6$ is not even." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186407649} {:answer/id #uuid "9ccbc68f-f80e-568d-9af1-dbe5b040a3d8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "If $6$ is even, then $3$ divides $6.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186407650} {:answer/id #uuid "d67594ef-42cc-5ae7-bb86-e6ecd7ab3420" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "If $6$ is not even, then $3$ doesn't divide $6.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186407659}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186407646} :answer-field/id #uuid "6f850b69-588c-535b-85d5-0554bb105429" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186407663}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "eca4be9a-a852-52a1-8e8c-2e200b9d2794" :question/math-academy-id "q-183274" :question/problem "Find the inverse of the following statement: \n\n$\\,$ **If** $3$ divides $6,$ **then** $6$ is even." :question/worked-solution "In our conditional statement:\n\n- The antecedent is $A:$ $3$ divides $6.$\n\n- The consequent is $B:$ $6$ is even.\n\nThe inverse of a conditional statement $A⇒B$ is given by \n\n$$\n¬A⇒¬B.\n$$\n\nFirst, we write down the negations of $A$ and $B:$\n\n- $¬A:$ $3$ doesn't divide $6.$\n\n- $¬B:$ $6$ is not even.\n\nTherefore, the inverse is the following: \n\n$\\,$ If $3$ doesn't divide $6,$ then $6$ is not even."} :step/id #uuid "9864b616-65d6-5ca3-a7e3-49b7953da8ad" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186407676}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186407674 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186407671 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "07403375-0a14-5e0c-9b83-f1f7a1d8d5eb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "If $4>6,$ then ${0}⊄{1,2,3}.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186407637} {:answer/id #uuid "41036f0e-f48f-54b0-ad45-917785a0ae65" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "If ${0}⊄{1,2,3},$ then $4>6.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186407642} {:answer/id #uuid "4b732aa6-c0fa-544f-860e-c7f782bacec2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "If $4\\le 6,$ then ${0}⊄{1,2,3}.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186407643} {:answer/id #uuid "a4fd80e3-a875-5579-b274-b169a9611ea3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "If ${0}⊄{1,2,3},$ then $4\\le 6.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186407653} {:answer/id #uuid "cad940a3-7a30-5ff4-93a8-409b9be10a0f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "If $4>6,$ then ${0}⊂{1,2,3}.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186407658}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186407643} :answer-field/id #uuid "e647ef76-2240-59c3-8c83-9a4ef59a40a3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186407665}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "fa1fdfba-09c3-560d-b8ff-6308784b3029" :question/math-academy-id "q-183337" :question/problem "Find the contrapositive of the following statement: \n\n$\\,$ **If** ${0}⊂{1,2,3},$ **then** $4>6.$" :question/worked-solution "In our conditional statement:\n\n- The antecedent is $A:$ ${0}⊂{1,2,3}.$\n\n- The consequent is $B:$ $4>6.$\n\nThe contrapositive of a conditional statement $A⇒B$ is given by \n\n$$\n¬B⇒¬A.\n$$\n\nFirst, we write down the negations of $A$ and $B:$\n\n- $¬A:$ ${0}⊄{1,2,3}.$\n\n- $¬B:$ $4\\le 6.$\n\nTherefore, the contrapositive is the following: \n\n$\\,$ If $4\\le 6,$ then ${0}⊄{1,2,3}.$"} :step/id #uuid "b4ffe877-52e1-50d0-9ff6-0d5690dd67b5" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186407675}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186407675 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186407667 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "71f417cf-0536-54c4-b46a-510edd2f3084" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472814} {:answer/id #uuid "74f27fa9-e14e-5a7b-a59d-e4f8f4f07523" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472815}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186472814} :answer-field/id #uuid "7c82116e-ddf7-523c-8827-05efd60ca46b" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473802} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8fb3e374-acff-5951-8e7b-106d3ee1d226" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472816} {:answer/id #uuid "29aae364-4c1b-55ea-b0c7-3b01642bf4c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472817}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186472816} :answer-field/id #uuid "5b6480a4-7991-54a8-8209-37a4015dd66a" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473803} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7dcb7e8d-cce0-53ff-95e0-c4e55ecc50af" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472818} {:answer/id #uuid "9c9dc198-f0b8-5675-bee7-c3bb6d3fd1d8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472819}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186472819} :answer-field/id #uuid "1e90f976-19af-5624-afdd-dbae7aa38b78" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473804}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "23603376-708c-5de8-b4d0-019ec40ac31f" :question/math-academy-id "q-183340" :question/problem "$\\,$ **If** $-2\\in Z,$ **then** $5$ is prime.\n\nWhich of the following statements are equivalent to the conditional statement above?\n- **I.** If $-2\\notin Z,$ then $5$ is not prime.\n- **II.** If $5$ is prime, then $-2\\in Z.$\n- **III.** If $5$ is not prime, then $-2\\notin Z.$\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "Let's recall the following facts:\n\n- The contrapositive is logically equivalent to the original statement.\n\n- The inverse and the converse are logically equivalent to each other, but not to the original statement.\n\n![](images/0d/0deb19675402bf931111bb80cb616682aac08491b5cd3e1ab5812da05b6df8a8.png)\n\nSo, we are looking for the contrapositive of the given statement.\n\n- Statement I is the inverse, not the contrapositive. $\\,\\times $\n\n- Statement II is the converse, not the contrapositive. $\\,\\times $\n\n- Statement III is the contrapositive. $\\,✓$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\""} :step/id #uuid "c7672cfc-51b1-5edd-a593-97ceb2928169"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186407676 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186407669 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "510c98ba-ef87-5fff-b4b1-e86de7cdfb0a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "If it is summer, then you go to the beach." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186407645} {:answer/id #uuid "9e2b2fc1-d648-5d31-a1bf-eb01219a5fe4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "If you don't go to the beach, then it is not summer" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186407651} {:answer/id #uuid "aa3283a3-cded-5b86-bf40-e38e5cd197ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "If it is not summer, then you go to the beach." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186407654} {:answer/id #uuid "c584f385-4eba-5ef1-a423-eac23cbae655" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "If you go to the beach, then it is summer" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186407657} {:answer/id #uuid "fb8ad54f-4913-5b36-8cdb-740da26e279e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "If it is summer, then you don't go to the beach." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186407660}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186407645} :answer-field/id #uuid "286c752f-2970-5ff4-abd2-b57ef3623964" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186407662}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "a480d9fc-6f80-5af5-b6f1-0b67fa2323fc" :question/math-academy-id "q-183281" :question/problem "Find the inverse of the following statement: \n\n$\\,$ **If** it is not summer, **then** you don't go to the beach." :question/worked-solution "In our conditional statement:\n\n- The antecedent is $A:$ It is not summer.\n\n- The consequent is $B:$ You don't go to the beach.\n\nThe inverse of a conditional statement $A⇒B$ is given by \n\n$$\n¬A⇒¬B.\n$$\n\nFirst, we write down the negations of $A$ and $B:$\n\n- $¬A:$ It is summer.\n\n- $¬B:$ You go to the beach.\n\nTherefore, the inverse is the following: \n\n$\\,$ If it is summer, then you go to the beach."} :step/id #uuid "f22856db-f661-53df-a19e-2bc1cf583961" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186407674}}] :activity/title "Converse, Inverse, and Contrapositive" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186407636}]}
